Z||000000||Ambush||09-17-2001||01:07 AM||||OK so far you guys have been a great help. It's now time for SUSPENSION!!!!<BR>I used KYB before (mustang) and i loved it. Im not the "racey" type but i do want my car a little stiifer than stock. Where can I buy some cool springs, shocks, and struts for my 86? SE 6cyl. Also doesanyone know where I can find some Nissan 300Zx headlight assemblies. I want to get rid of my pop up lights.<p>[This message has been edited by Ambush (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||02:05 AM||||I had a red 86 SE V6. Loved that car too. I like the four speed the most!<BR>I'm gonna change the suspension too. Not sure of what I will use or when. <P>300ZX headlights? <BR>Love to see a pic of that.<P>Good luck!!<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||09-17-2001||03:24 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>   aka RD Enterprises.  <BR>Got Tokico Blues for my T-bird there, for $200 a complete set.  They sell Koni and KYB as well.  Eibach (variable rate) springs just over $225 for the same car, Fiero probably the same or at least close.  <BR>Suspension Techniques springs (linear rate) $160 a set at JC Whitney.  I have them in my 86 GT, with poly bushings and Monroe Gasmatics, and they are a bit rough on the kidneys, but not unacceptable for a Fiero. Handling is great.<P>Summitt Racing carries KYB, Eibach, and Koni, also.<P>Get the Moog Problem Solver adjustable upper ball joints, so you can get it aligned properly.  Thet are only about $20-30 each, and well worth it.  And find a GOOD (patient)alignment shop.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-17-2001||05:13 AM||||Here's what I'm planning (once I have the cash).  Street Dreams spindles up front, Ground Control coil overs in the rear, KYB shocks and struts, 1" sway bar, and all poly bushings.  This should lower my car about 2" in the front and 2 1/2" in the rear (to level it out).  The ride should be similar to stock and should handle like a sled on rails.  Only problem is the cost.  I figure it'll be somewhere around $1200. <P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000004||Banzai||09-17-2001||08:57 AM||||I got with shox.com last week on lowering springs.  $219 for the Eibachs, they price matched the ST springs with Whitney for $160(their normal price was $199), they sell KYB's for 199 all around, and Koni's for $504 all around.  Ground Effects coil overs are $199 (rear only). They seemed very helpful and are haveing ST drop ship the springs--said I'd see em this week.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!||||reg||1
